  "chain": "I&C Techs fail to apply adequate force to seat manifold valve [cause TBD] -> manifold passes high pressure to common sensing line -> multiple trip units perturbated into gross fail -> spurious Division 2 Level 1 initiation signal -> inadvertent RHR B/LPCI actuation and injection into RCS (RHR C blocked by LSS out of service; Shutdown Cooling remained in operation)",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Official cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; category left as 'provisional' per rule 4, despite narrative clearly describing a personnel-error causal chain. RHR C did not actually inject because Division 2 LSS was out of service for SSW B flow balancing, preventing RHR C and Division 2 DG start — this is plant-condition context, not a backup system that mitigated the event, so no BACKED_UP_BY edge was created; Shutdown Cooling remaining in operation is noted as context in the consequence chain but not modeled as a formal backup system since it is not an ECCS/ordinarily-invoked mitigation for this actuation. Block 13 was empty (all NA) in FORM-366 fields, consistent with no reportable component failure being coded."
